# lit-retry.py (plan 5.17.9, M24): 'select <xunit> [--max N]' prints the full
# names of the timeout-only failed tests of a lit run, one per line. A failed
# test is timeout-only when the part of its xunit failure text after the last
# '# executed command:' line (the command at which lit's internal shell
# stopped) holds a timeout marker. It exits 0 when every failed test is
# timeout-only and at most N (default 3) are, 3 when more are, 4 when a
# failure is not timeout-only, and 2 on a usage error or a file it cannot
# read. timeout-retry.test checks how lit-legs.ps1 uses it.
# (1) --self-test passes every case.
# (2) On the xunit files of nested lit runs of Inputs/nested-retry, whose
# tests fail at their last command with each kind of marker (msil-run.py's and
# msil-verify.py's 'did not finish within <T> s', the transcript status line
# [timeout], msil-prog.py's '(timeout after <T> s)'), fail without one, with
# one only in an earlier command's output, or with one only on the last
# command's own line, and pass with one: (a) every test: exit 4, naming
# exactly the three failures that are not timeout-only; (b) --filter=timeout
# (lit lists the others as skipped): exit 3 with the default --max, exit 0
# with --max 4, printing the four names; (c) one timeout and the passing test:
# exit 0, that one name; (d) the passing test alone: exit 0, no name.
# (3) A missing file, a file that is not XML and usage errors exit 2.
# (4) A harness test that runs lit inside lit (M27; plan section 12, row
# 'M27.d extended (P-1b leftover: timeouts inside nested lit runs)'): the
# outer failure text quotes the nested run's output with a second level of
# lit's '# | ' prefix. Synthetic xunit files with one failed test each:
# (a) after the last '# executed command:' a check of a nested log whose
# run ended in the transcript line '+[timeout]', printed as
# '# | # | +[timeout]': timeout-only, so select exits 0 naming the test;
# (b) the same nested failure with a transcript that differs in its status
# instead ('-[exit 0]', '+[exit 1]') and no timeout marker: not timeout-only,
# exit 4 naming it.

